<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Distance is one factor that influences the travel time of Priya’s car trips. What are some other factors?</item>
</list>

    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">

  <item>Which of these factors (including distance) most likely has the most consistent influence for all the car trips? Be prepared to show your reasoning.
    </item>
</list>
    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Create the scatter plot and calculate the best fit line using the Desmos tool below.   </item>
</list>
<para>(Students were provided access to Desmos.)</para>
    <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
      <figure><media alt="Scatter plot with line of best fit.  "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5d012ead5546eb746e7d588e1a33558ce4083141"/></media></figure><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>What do the slope and \(y\)-intercept for the line of best fit mean in this situation?
